# GlobeTrotter — API Contract v1.1

---

## 1. Problem Recap

GlobeTrotter is a personalized travel-planning platform where authenticated users create multi-city trip itineraries, add stops (cities) with date ranges, attach activities to each stop, and track budgets. The app provides a dashboard with upcoming trips, a city/activity discovery search, cost breakdowns with charts, a calendar/timeline view of itineraries, and the ability to share itineraries publicly. An optional admin analytics dashboard tracks platform-wide usage. The core user flow is: **sign up → dashboard → create trip → add stops (cities + dates) → add activities per stop → review itinerary/budget → share**.

---

## 2. Assumptions & Open Questions

| # | Item | Default Chosen |
|---|------|---------------|
| 1 | **Persistence** | SQLite via SQLAlchemy. All models map to relational tables. |
| 2 | **Auth mechanism** | Email + password with JWT access tokens (problem statement explicitly requires login/signup). Tokens sent as `Authorization: Bearer <token>`. |
| 3 | **IDs** | `str` (UUID4) for all primary keys. |
| 4 | **Cover photo upload** | Accepted as a URL string (not multipart upload) in MVP. |
| 5 | **"Copy Trip" on shared page** | Creates a full deep-copy of the trip under the copying user's account. |
| 6 | **City & Activity catalogues** | Pre-seeded reference data. Users search/filter but don't create cities/activities — they *add* catalogue items to their stops. |
| 7 | **Budget** | Derived server-side by summing activity costs + stop-level transport/stay costs. No separate "budget" entity; it's a computed view. |
| 8 | **Reordering stops/activities** | Handled via an `order` integer field; client sends updated order values. |
| 9 | **"Forgot Password"** | Out of scope for MVP — endpoint stub only. |
| 10 | **Admin dashboard** | Guarded by an `is_admin` flag on the user. |
| 11 | **Language preference** | Stored as a string on the user profile; no i18n in MVP. |
| 12 | **Social media sharing** | Frontend-only (share URL); no server-side integration. |
| 13 | **Currency** | All costs are stored and displayed in **INR (₹)** only. No multi-currency support in MVP. |
| 14 | **Privacy levels for shared trips** | Two levels only: `public` and `private`. No `friends_only` in MVP. |

