## 3. Data Models

### 3.1 User

```python
class UserBase(BaseModel):
    email: str                        # unique, required
    name: str                         # display name, required

class UserCreate(UserBase):
    password: str                     # required, min 8 chars

class UserUpdate(BaseModel):
    name: str | None = None
    email: str | None = None
    photo_url: str | None = None
    language_preference: str | None = None   # e.g. "en", "es"

class UserOut(UserBase):
    id: str                           # UUID
    photo_url: str | None = None
    language_preference: str = "en"
    is_admin: bool = False
    created_at: str                   # ISO 8601
```

### 3.2 Trip

```python
class TripCreate(BaseModel):
    name: str                         # required
    description: str | None = None
    start_date: str                   # ISO 8601 date, e.g. "2026-09-01"
    end_date: str                     # ISO 8601 date
    cover_photo_url: str | None = None
    is_public: bool = False           # shareable?

class TripUpdate(BaseModel):
    name: str | None = None
    description: str | None = None
    start_date: str | None = None
    end_date: str | None = None
    cover_photo_url: str | None = None
    is_public: bool | None = None

class TripOut(BaseModel):
    id: str                           # UUID
    user_id: str
    name: str
    description: str | None = None
    start_date: str
    end_date: str
    cover_photo_url: str | None = None
    is_public: bool
    stop_count: int                   # computed
    total_estimated_cost: float       # computed sum, in INR (₹)
    created_at: str
    updated_at: str
```

### 3.3 Stop (a city within a trip)

```python
class StopCreate(BaseModel):
    city_id: str                      # references City catalogue
    arrival_date: str                 # ISO 8601 date
    departure_date: str
    transport_cost: float = 0.0       # cost to reach this stop, in INR (₹)
    stay_cost: float = 0.0            # accommodation cost, in INR (₹)
    order: int                        # display order within trip

class StopUpdate(BaseModel):
    arrival_date: str | None = None
    departure_date: str | None = None
    transport_cost: float | None = None
    stay_cost: float | None = None
    order: int | None = None

class StopOut(BaseModel):
    id: str                           # UUID
    trip_id: str
    city_id: str
    city_name: str                    # denormalized for convenience
    country: str                      # denormalized
    arrival_date: str
    departure_date: str
    transport_cost: float
    stay_cost: float
    order: int
    activities: list[StopActivityOut] # nested
    total_cost: float                 # transport + stay + sum(activity costs)
```

### 3.4 StopActivity (an activity assigned to a stop)

```python
class StopActivityCreate(BaseModel):
    activity_id: str                  # references Activity catalogue
    date: str                         # ISO 8601 date (must be within stop date range)
    start_time: str | None = None     # "09:00"
    end_time: str | None = None       # "11:00"
    order: int = 0                    # order within the day

class StopActivityUpdate(BaseModel):
    date: str | None = None
    start_time: str | None = None
    end_time: str | None = None
    order: int | None = None

class StopActivityOut(BaseModel):
    id: str                           # UUID
    stop_id: str
    activity_id: str
    activity_name: str                # denormalized
    category: str                     # denormalized
    estimated_cost: float             # from catalogue, in INR (₹)
    date: str
    start_time: str | None
    end_time: str | None
    order: int
    image_url: str | None             # from catalogue
    description: str | None           # from catalogue
```

